BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 740 Td
(Sample Paper on Diffusion Distillation) Tj T*
(Abstract. We study distillation of diffusion models into few-step generators.) Tj T*
(Our method reduces sampling cost by a factor of eight while keeping image quality.) Tj T*
(1 Introduction) Tj T*
(Diffusion models produce high quality samples but require many network evaluations.) Tj T*
(Distillation compresses the sampling trajectory into a small number of steps.) Tj T*
(We propose a progressive scheme that halves the number of steps at every stage.) Tj T*
(2 Method) Tj T*
(A student network is trained to match two teacher steps with one student step.) Tj T*
(The procedure is repeated until the student needs only four steps in total.) Tj T*
(3 Experiments) Tj T*
(We evaluate on ImageNet and report FID against the undistilled teacher baseline.) Tj T*
(The distilled model achieves an eight times speedup with a small FID increase.) Tj T*
(Ablations show that the loss weighting matters more than the schedule choice.) Tj T*
(4 Conclusion) Tj T*
(Progressive distillation offers a simple recipe for fast sampling from diffusion models.) Tj T*
(References) Tj T*
([1] Ho et al. Denoising diffusion probabilistic models.) Tj T*
ET
